\pard\qc\f0\fs32\b AI Usage Declaration\b0\par
\pard\sa240\qc\fs22 COMP5050 Programming Assignment 2\par
\pard\sa180\fs24 This statement records the generative AI assistance used in the planning, implementation, and verification of this assignment.\par
\pard\sa120\fs24\b Entry 1  Planning and concept clarification\b0\par
\pard\sa80\fs24\b 1.1 AI version used.\b0\par
\pard\li360\sa140\fs24 OpenAI Codex, a GPT-5-based coding agent.\par
\pard\sa80\fs24\b 1.2 When was it used.\b0\par
\pard\li360\sa140\fs24 15 September 2026, during requirements analysis and Petri-net planning.\par
\pard\sa80\fs24\b 1.3 How did it help with the assignment.\b0\par
\pard\li360\sa200\fs24 The tool analysed the supplied brief, diagrams, interface, and course materials. It identified the eight permitted routes, mapped the public API requirements, and helped construct the Petri-net places, transitions, guards, priority rule, and safety invariants. It also recorded requirements that still depend on the final GitHub submission process.\par
\pard\sa120\fs24\b Entry 2  Code generation and testing\b0\par
\pard\sa80\fs24\b 2.1 AI version used.\b0\par
\pard\li360\sa140\fs24 OpenAI Codex, a GPT-5-based coding agent.\par
\pard\sa80\fs24\b 2.2 When was it used.\b0\par
\pard\li360\sa140\fs24 15 September 2026, during implementation, test construction, and final review.\par
\pard\sa80\fs24\b 2.3 How did it help with the assignment.\b0\par
\pard\li360\sa180\fs24 The tool generated and refined InterlockingImpl.java and the JUnit 4 test suite. It checked simultaneous movement, section occupancy, passenger priority, invalid inputs, all legal routes, exit behaviour, and deterministic conflict handling. The completed files were compiled with JDK 11, all 39 tests were run successfully, and coverage was measured before delivery.\par
